{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R14", "R15"],
      "pins": ["U1.8"],
      "nets": ["0V8_BK", "+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the POWER TRAIN sheet the TPS62933 (U1) feedback divider is drawn as R14 = 5.1k from the +5V output to the FB/0V8_BK node and R15 = 10k from FB to GND (a top/bottom ratio of only ~0.51; even if the two are read the other way round the ratio is ~1.96).",
      "expected": "The feedback node is named 0V8_BK (0.8 V reference), so Vout = 0.8 x (1 + Rtop/Rbot). For the specified +5 V rail the ratio must be ~5.25 (e.g. Rtop = 51k with Rbot = 10k, or 5.1k with 1k). The drawn 5.1k/10k pair is ~10x too low.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 TPS62933 ... FB 8 ... R14 5.1k ... R15 10k ... (Power Train, sheet 1)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U1 — TPS62933 (TI) | 24 V → 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A ... feedback via R13/R14/R15"}
      ],
      "impact": "The +5V rail would regulate to roughly 0.8 x (1 + 5.1/10) ≈ 1.2 V instead of 5 V. The ESP32-C6 DevKit (5V0 pin), the AZ1117-3.3 LDO and therefore the whole +3V3 domain would be starved, so the board would not start.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["H6", "PR6", "C29", "C31"],
      "pins": ["H6.1"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "I2C_SCL", "I2C_SDA"],
      "observed": "The optional environmental-sensor header H6 (for the BME280, PR6) has its VCC pin tied to the +5V rail, while the light-sensor header H5 is tied to +3V3.",
      "expected": "The specification states both 4-pin JST-PH I2C headers break out the same rail: 'H5, H6 (4-pin JST-PH headers) — each breaks out +3V3, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA.' H6 should therefore be on +3V3 like H5.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Environmental Sensor (optional) ... H6 JST_PH ... +5V (sheet 1, I2C SENSORS block)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "H5, H6 (4-pin JST-PH headers) — each breaks out +3V3, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA."}
      ],
      "impact": "A 3.3V-only BME280 (or bare sensor) plugged into H6 would be over-powered, while the 3.3V I2C bus pull-ups (R3/R4) remain referenced to +3V3; this is a level/power mismatch for that header.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing is largely consistent with the specification, but the TPS62933 feedback divider (R14 = 5.1k / R15 = 10k) sets the '5V' rail to about 1.2 V instead of 5 V, which would prevent the board from powering up; a secondary deviation is the optional BME280 header H6 being tied to +5V rather than the +3V3 stated in the spec."
}

